  "review": [
    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "note": "Standard Sinhala past/to system: '{h}යි' (තුනයි = it's three), '{h}යි කාලයි' (quarter past), '{h} හමාරයි' (half past), '{next_h}ට කාලයි' (quarter to, next hour in dative), '{next_h}ට විනාඩි දහයයි' (ten to). Minute phrases include විනාඩි so 'තුනයි පහයි' cannot be misread as 'three and five'. Compromise: 'හමාරයි' is written with a space ('තුන හමාරයි') rather than fused ('තුනහමාරයි') because the fused form has sandhi for hours ending in හ (පහමාරයි, එකොළහමාරයි, දොළහමාරයි) that a single template cannot produce; the spaced form is understood and attested in informal writing but the fused spelling is the more usual one. Both '{h}යි' and '{h}ට' attach cleanly to all 12 hour names."
    }
  ]
